CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*pcc_data[pcc_ss_id])...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct cppc_pcc_data)...)
#409: FILE: drivers/acpi/cppc_acpi.c:638:
+	pcc_data[pcc_ss_id] = kzalloc(sizeof(struct cppc_pcc_data), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

